-- <msg:7> helper (html)
   | <!-- codex-helper-outbox:<marker> --><p><strong>🔧 Helper:</strong></p>
   | <p><strong>🏠 Control chat advanced help</strong></p>
   | <p>Workspace flow:</p>
   | <ul><li><code>p</code> / <code>projects</code> - list directories with local Codex history</li>
   | <li><code>p 1</code> / <code>project 1</code> / <code>1</code> - open workspace 1 from the <code>projects</code> list</li>
   | <li><code>new</code> / <code>n</code> - create a Work chat in the currently opened workspace</li>
   | <li><code>n &lt;directory&gt;</code> / <code>new &lt;directory&gt;</code> - create the directory if missing, then create a Work chat there</li>
   | </ul>
   | <p>History flow:</p>
   | <ul><li><code>s</code> / <code>sessions</code> / <code>history</code> - list local sessions in the selected workspace</li>
   | <li><code>c 1</code> / <code>continue 1</code> / <code>1</code> on a sessions page - create/open a Work chat and import that session history</li>
   | </ul>
   | <p>Other control commands:</p>
   | <ul><li><code>st</code> / <code>status</code> - list active Teams work chats</li>
   | <li><code>d &lt;number&gt;</code> / <code>details &lt;number&gt;</code> - show technical IDs and details</li>
   | <li><code>park &lt;session-number-or-id&gt;</code> / <code>resume &lt;session-number-or-id&gt;</code> / <code>unpark &lt;session-number-or-id&gt;</code> - manually pause or resume polling for a Work chat</li>
   | <li><code>fork &lt;session&gt;</code> - copy a session into a new Work chat</li>
   | <li><code>m &lt;directory&gt;</code> / <code>mkdir &lt;directory&gt;</code> - create a directory only</li>
   | <li><code>ask &lt;question&gt;</code> - ask a quick helper question in this control chat</li>
   | <li><code>helper cancel last</code> / <code>helper cancel queued</code> / <code>helper cancel running</code> / <code>helper cancel all</code> - stop queued/running Codex question(s) in this Control chat</li>
   | <li><code>model status|list|switch|reset</code> and <code>effort status|list|set|reset</code> - inspect or change only this Control chat (<code>model use</code> aliases switch)</li>
   | <li>Control-only <code>default model ...</code> / <code>default effort ...</code> manage future global defaults</li>
   | <li><code>helper rename &lt;title&gt;</code> - rename this Control chat</li>
   | <li><code>helper rename hostname &lt;name&gt;</code> - rename this machine in the Control chat and all linked Work chats</li>
   | <li><code>h</code> / <code>help</code> / <code>menu</code> - show short help</li>
   | <li><code>helper restart</code> - show the safe restart confirmation</li>
   | <li><code>helper restart now</code> - restart the local Teams helper after sending a confirmation</li>
   | <li><code>shutdown</code> - stop the helper on all machines until <code>cxp teams start</code> is run on a machine</li>
   | <li><code>helper update now</code> - update to the latest stable helper release</li>
   | <li><code>helper update prerelease</code> - update to the newest helper release or pre-release</li>
   | <li><code>codex update now</code> - wait for active work, then update the local Codex CLI</li>
   | <li><code>helper webhook setup</code> - show a guided Workflow webhook setup flow</li>
   | <li><code>helper webhook &lt;url&gt;</code> - enable Workflow notification cards with a Teams Workflow webhook URL</li>
   | <li><code>helper webhook off</code> - disable Workflow notification cards</li>
   | <li><code>helper skills list|add|sync|push</code> - manage skill subscriptions</li>
   | </ul>
   | <p>Local CLI:</p>
   | <ul><li><code>cxp teams stop</code> / <code>cxp teams start</code> - stop the helper on all machines / start it again</li>
   | <li><code>cxp skills install-builtin</code> - install or repair bundled local skills in <code>$HOME/.agents/skills</code></li>
   | <li><code>cxp skills migrate</code> - migrate managed legacy skills from <code>~/.codex/skills</code> to <code>$HOME/.agents/skills</code></li>
   | </ul>
   | <p>work chat commands:<br>
   | Inside a 💬 Work chat, send your task as a regular Teams message. Use <code>helper help</code>, <code>helper status</code>, <code>helper stats</code>, <code>helper retry last</code>, <code>helper file &lt;relative-path&gt;</code>, or <code>helper close</code> for helper actions.<br>
   | Status words: <code>queued</code>/<code>running</code> means wait, <code>completed</code> means done, <code>failed</code> or <code>interrupted</code> means check recent messages and changed files before <code>helper retry last</code>.<br>
   | If this chat stops replying for about a minute, send <code>helper status</code>. From the control chat, <code>helper restart now</code> restarts the installed helper.</p>
   | <p>copy-ready examples:<br>
   | <code>p</code><br>
   | <code>n /home/baka/project/codex-helper</code><br>
   | <code>m ~<tmp:1></code></p>

